<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falco</span></b> , ōnis, m.
		v. flecto, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάλκων</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a falcon.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A.
				10, 146</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 12, 7, 57
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: falcones dicuntur, quorum digiti
			pollices in pedibus intro sunt curvati, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				88, 8</span></i> Müll.; cf. falcula, II. A.</div>
